From 0c370b7c08e70c6d444799bcb7cb93d4c7d99593 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 116/118] wifi: ath10k: handle the DROP HTT tx completion
 status

The WCN3990 firmware reports HTT tx completion status 5 when it drops an
MSDU for lack of buffer space. enum htt_data_tx_status only names values
0..3, so ath10k_htt_rx_tx_compl_ind() takes the default: branch and logs

  ath10k_snoc 18800000.wifi: unhandled tx completion status 5

for every such completion indication. The MSDU itself is already handled
correctly - the default: branch maps it to HTT_TX_COMPL_STATE_DISCARD, so
the skb is unmapped and reported to mac80211 with the ACK flag cleared -
but the message says the driver does not understand a code that is in
fact documented, and it is emitted unthrottled, once per completion
indication, for as long as the firmware keeps dropping.

The status code is HTT_TX_COMPL_IND_STAT_DROP in the vendor fw-api
htt.h ("MSDUs dropped due to lack of space (congestion control)"). Name
it and map it to the discard case, next to the other two statuses that
mean "this MSDU was not transmitted".

This was found on a Pixel 2 XL (msm8998, WCN3990 hw1.0) where the
firmware stopped accepting transmit frames on an idle station link: every
data frame, including the supplicant's EAPOL frames, came back with
status 5, so eight successive associations reached the associated state
and none reached the 4-way handshake.

Note that HTT_TX_COMPL_IND_STAT_PEER_DEL (4) and
HTT_TX_COMPL_IND_STAT_HOST_INSPECT (6) are deliberately left out: they
are not emitted by any firmware this driver has been seen to talk to,
and commit 30e7099a6dc9 ("wifi: ath10k: drop
HTT_DATA_TX_STATUS_DOWNLOAD_FAIL") established that unused values do not
belong in this enum.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt.h    | 9 ++++++++-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt_rx.c | 1 +
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt.h
index 603f6de62b0a..7b998c663727 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt.h
@@ -881,7 +881,14 @@ enum htt_data_tx_status {
 	HTT_DATA_TX_STATUS_OK            = 0,
 	HTT_DATA_TX_STATUS_DISCARD       = 1,
 	HTT_DATA_TX_STATUS_NO_ACK        = 2,
-	HTT_DATA_TX_STATUS_POSTPONE      = 3 /* HL only */
+	HTT_DATA_TX_STATUS_POSTPONE      = 3, /* HL only */
+
+	/* The firmware dropped the MSDU because it had no space for it. The
+	 * frame is gone for good, unlike POSTPONE the host is not expected to
+	 * download it again. Seen on WCN3990 when the firmware wedges and
+	 * stops accepting transmit frames altogether.
+	 */
+	HTT_DATA_TX_STATUS_DROP          = 5
 };
 
 enum htt_data_tx_flags {
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt_rx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt_rx.c
index d7e429041065..88f9ba3a2927 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/htt_rx.c
@@ -2969,6 +2969,7 @@ static void ath10k_htt_rx_tx_compl_ind(struct ath10k *ar,
 		break;
 	case HTT_DATA_TX_STATUS_DISCARD:
 	case HTT_DATA_TX_STATUS_POSTPONE:
+	case HTT_DATA_TX_STATUS_DROP:
 		tx_done.status = HTT_TX_COMPL_STATE_DISCARD;
 		break;
 	default:
